    "The atomic convention counts whole-document whitespace tokens and alphanumeric runs at their first character, and assigns collapsed whitespace to the owner of its initial character. UTF-8 bytes and nonspace characters belong to their unique owner. Normalization is explicitly tested not to cross a boundary.",
    "All five adopted units are additive under NFC and NFKC. The independent character-mask/state-counter implementation matches every one of the 3370 owner cells and the 140 whole-document cells without importing the author accounting implementation.",
    "The four required computational nodes reference one code.appendix owner. The entire printed four-file appendix is paid once, with full raw-code inclusion verified. Raw files are alternative representations, not additional simultaneous charges.",
    "The current common-paper PDF is the accepted retraction edition, and A6 is the accepted one-sentence attribution edition. Their exact byte bindings match the numerical integration.",
    "External theorem proofs and historical computational inputs have null dependency costs. Unextracted scientific image text and diagram structure remain null; no numeric zero or full-visible-content claim is introduced."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The closure subtotals are documentary known-text subtotals, not complete dependency costs, minimal proofs or new compression factors. The owner ledger explicitly lists other text in the same documents outside each closure.",
    "Owner categories and theorem/branch granularity are descriptive. A context owner may contain immediately attached connective prose, and some ancillary statements remain outside named output closures while fully charged to their documents.",
    "L035 image labels/diagrams and the clipped last-page image remain unmeasured. Historical external programs and retained proof libraries do not become free through this partition.",
